```sql
INSTALL ducklake;
INSTALL postgres;
-- Ensure the database 'ducklake_catalog' exists in PostgreSQL
ATTACH 'ducklake:postgres:dbname=ducklake_catalog host=localhost' AS my_ducklake (DATA_PATH 'data_files/');
USE my_ducklake;
```
This creates or attaches a DuckLake catalog using PostgreSQL for metadata and the specified path for Parquet data files. For details, see [Choosing a Catalog Database – DuckLake](https://ducklake.select/docs/stable/duckdb/usage/choosing_a_catalog_database).

Multiple DuckDB processes can write concurrently to the same DuckLake catalog when using PostgreSQL, as it is a transactional client-server database designed for multi-user access. This is not possible with DuckDB as the catalog, which only supports a single client. See [Choosing a Catalog Database – DuckLake](https://ducklake.select/docs/stable/duckdb/usage/choosing_a_catalog_database).

